            {
              "id": "511b5113-bbb4-4cc1-8f99-641785cb9228",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Otaku: Japan’s Database Animals</strong></em> was written by Hiroki Azuma, published by University Of Minnesota Press, March 25, 2009."
            },
            {
              "id": "f7c907e0-9f05-49aa-be20-863a9b17bd32",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "010a29f2-eabf-49ab-a21f-1baf5b0dbde8",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>In Japan, obsessive adult fans and collectors of manga and anime are known as otaku. Hiroki Azuma's 'Otaku' offers a critical, philosophical, and historical inquiry into the characteristics and consequences of this consumer subculture.</em>"
            },
            {
